(5701573, 829545, 33672, '<td valign="top">I love this place!</td>', 'I love this place!', '2009-10-26 21:57:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701575, 829594, 56828, '<td valign="top">I think your tilt hurt the photo some.  Because of your tilt I found my eyes quickly following the path of the bridge off the picture.</td>', 'I think your tilt hurt the photo some.  Because of your tilt I found my eyes quickly following the path of the bridge off the picture.', '2009-10-26 21:57:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701579, 829547, 56828, '<td valign="top">Okay definitely not Deep DOF.  Probably more of shallow DOF.  You could have also used soft focus.  The soft focus of the photo is making me like it more.  The black and white is good also.  I think her nose and under her eyes should be toned down some though. I know it''s use of high key, but it looks as if it went just a tad bit too far.</td>', 'Okay definitely not Deep DOF.  Probably more of shallow DOF.  You could have also used soft focus.  The soft focus of the photo is making me like it more.  The black and white is good also.  I think her nose and under her eyes should be toned down some though. I know it''s use of high key, but it looks as if it went just a tad bit too far.', '2009-10-26 22:01:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701585, 828907, 56828, '<td valign="top">Center Composition, Leading Lines, ????.    Judging the photo itself, the plane is a distraction.  You can''t determine which is your actual subject, the plane or the building.<br/> <br/>Edited: Took a second look at the shot and bumped it up 2 points.</td>', 'Center Composition, Leading Lines, ????.    Judging the photo itself, the plane is a distraction.  You can''t determine which is your actual subject, the plane or the building. Edited: Took a second look at the shot and bumped it up 2 points.', '2009-10-26 22:07:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701586, 829144, 36981, '<td valign="top">Oh, I''m sorry.  I''m sure you''re regretting the title so I won''t hammer on that.  I see for the challenge: rule of thirds, blur, long exposure.  Well done on using 3 techniques.  Even so, I think the image is nice but doesn''t move me in any way emotionally, so a 6 from me.</td>', 'Oh, I''m sorry.  I''m sure you''re regretting the title so I won''t hammer on that.  I see for the challenge: rule of thirds, blur, long exposure.  Well done on using 3 techniques.  Even so, I think the image is nice but doesn''t move me in any way emotionally, so a 6 from me.', '2009-10-26 22:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701587, 828468, 56828, '<td valign="top">Looks closer to center composition, but I think this is a great shot.  I think the use of the open door as a light is just a great touch to it.  Sometimes simple is so much better.</td>', 'Looks closer to center composition, but I think this is a great shot.  I think the use of the open door as a light is just a great touch to it.  Sometimes simple is so much better.', '2009-10-26 22:10:29.000000', NULL, 1),
