(5701594, 829555, 56828, '<td valign="top">I think your tilt is a little extreme (but I''ve said that about quite a few tilts).  I don''t know what that glaring line across the photo is from but it''s really hurting this photo as well as the huge glare off the left window.  And even without the tilt, i''m not a big fan of the crop, but the crop seems to me as if it were because of the tilt done in post processing.</td>', 'I think your tilt is a little extreme (but I''ve said that about quite a few tilts).  I don''t know what that glaring line across the photo is from but it''s really hurting this photo as well as the huge glare off the left window.  And even without the tilt, i''m not a big fan of the crop, but the crop seems to me as if it were because of the tilt done in post processing.', '2009-10-26 22:15:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701595, 829158, 36981, '<td valign="top">A truly beautiful image.  I find this challenge exhausting to vote on (I don''t love having to pay such attention to either techniques or titles) but I hit my 20% so I wanted to come back to this one, which I find very peaceful &amp; relaxing.  Thank you!</td>', 'A truly beautiful image.  I find this challenge exhausting to vote on (I don''t love having to pay such attention to either techniques or titles) but I hit my 20% so I wanted to come back to this one, which I find very peaceful & relaxing.  Thank you!', '2009-10-26 22:15:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701596, 829458, 72103, '<td valign="top">Beautiful................! 9</td>', 'Beautiful................! 9', '2009-10-26 22:15:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701597, 828992, 56828, '<td valign="top">Best photo in the challenge.  This is just great.  Words could do it no justice.</td>', 'Best photo in the challenge.  This is just great.  Words could do it no justice.', '2009-10-26 22:17:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701599, 829012, 103142, '<td valign="top">There''s a couple of things that don''t work quite right in this photo. This really is almost exactly between rule of thirds and centered. If you would have cropped from the right a little, it would have worked for centered, if you would have cropped in from the left, it would have worked better for rule of thirds.<br/> <br/>This is a wonderful photo--I like the weeds in the front and the shallow depth of field. But the pine tree is very distracting and it seems a tad dark. I hope you don''t mind, but I liked the photo so much, I brought it into photoshop so I could suggest a crop and lighten it a tad. This is what I would suggest: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=829756" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/103142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_829756.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/103142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_829756.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/103142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_829756.jpg"/></a>. I just cropped it and adjusted slide in levels. (I actually would have the bird more off center, but with cropping out the tree, you can''t really get the rule of thirds). <br/> <br/>Feel free to completely ignore this if you disagree. It was just a suggestion because the shot really called to me. Good luck with the challenge!  :D</td>', 'There''s a couple of things that don''t work quite right in this photo. This really is almost exactly between rule of thirds and centered. If you would have cropped from the right a little, it would have worked for centered, if you would have cropped in from the left, it would have worked better for rule of thirds. This is a wonderful photo--I like the weeds in the front and the shallow depth of field. But the pine tree is very distracting and it seems a tad dark. I hope you don''t mind, but I liked the photo so much, I brought it into photoshop so I could suggest a crop and lighten it a tad. This is what I would suggest: . I just cropped it and adjusted slide in levels. (I actually would have the bird more off center, but with cropping out the tree, you can''t really get the rule of thirds).  Feel free to completely ignore this if you disagree. It was just a suggestion because the shot really called to me. Good luck with the challenge!  :D', '2009-10-26 22:17:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5701600, 828685, 36981, '<td valign="top">Superior - I generally dislike both centered comps &amp; tilts, but this is really great.  His face is so expressive, and you captured him well. (The white of his eyes are a little too white for me - I''d prefer if they blended a bit like his shirt color, but perhaps it was the eyes that drew me in to begin with)</td>', 'Superior - I generally dislike both centered comps & tilts, but this is really great.  His face is so expressive, and you captured him well. (The white of his eyes are a little too white for me - I''d prefer if they blended a bit like his shirt color, but perhaps it was the eyes that drew me in to begin with)', '2009-10-26 22:18:35.000000', NULL, 1),
